{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfdis2zVRSVUK96BbPGok","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I challenged B08 against `agent/` and found no failing check. I wrote `verdict.json` with an **upheld** verdict, and it parses as valid JSON.\n\n- **B08.1 holds.** The NetworkPolicy at `k8s/deployment.yaml:168` selects every pod in the namespace and covers both ingress and egress.\n  - Ingress is allowed only from the `ingress` namespace on port 8080.\n  - Egress goes only to kube-dns, the platform egress proxy on port 3128, and `10.60.12.0/28` on port 443.\n  - There is no `0.0.0.0/0`.\n- **B08.2 holds.**\n  - Pod egress is limited to the proxy, DNS and the /28, so pods can't reach `169.254.169.254`.\n  - The node group requires IMDSv2 with a hop limit of 1.\n  - `hostNetwork`, `hostPID` and `hostIPC` are false, and I found no `hostPath` or `docker.sock`.\n  - The EKS endpoint is private.\n  - The runtime IAM role is scoped to `clinic-agent-*` resources.\n- **B08.3 holds.** Isolation comes from the NetworkPolicy, the restricted Pod Security labels, the VPC and IAM. None of it depends on the prompt or on harness code.\n\nTwo things I couldn't settle from this repo:\n- **Egress proxy allow-list:** it lives outside this repo (in the `platform` namespace), so I took the comments' word for what it permits.\n- **Control table:** the runtime role can write the control table, which holds the operators' stop flags. I treated that as outside this check. It may belong under another item."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":976,"cache_read_input_tokens":18621,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":976},"output_tokens":555,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"se